---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CODE_FUNCTIONS, FUNCTIONS } from '../../data/catalog.mjs';
const questionFile = FUNCTIONS.find((f) => f.notAFunction);
---
<Base title="Functions" description="The ten functions, simplest first.">
  <h1>The ten functions</h1>
  <p class="lede">The model answers three kinds of question: yes or no, pick one, and place on a scale. Each function is one of those, shaped for a job you already know. They run simplest first, and the ones that read many records come after the ones that read a single text.</p>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Function</th><th>What it does</th><th>Primitive</th></tr>
    {CODE_FUNCTIONS.map((fn) => (
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`/functions/${fn.name}/`}><code>{fn.name}</code></a></td>
        <td>{fn.line}</td>
        <td>{fn.primitive}</td>
      </tr>
    ))}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="/functions/question-file/"><code>@question</code></a></td>
      <td>{questionFile.line}</td>
      <td>Not a function</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p>A question file is not counted as a function. A function gives an answer. A question file gives none. It is a saved question every function accepts.</p>

  <p class="pagelinks"><a href="/surfaces/">Every surface</a> · <a href="/how-tos/">How-tos</a></p>
</Base>
